> After the martyrdom of St. Boniface[, Ver]gili[us was made Bishop of] Salzburg ([7]66 or 767[) and] lab[oured successfully for the] up[building of his] di[ocese] as[ well as for the] spread[ of the Faith in neighbouring] heat[hen countries],[ especially in] Carinthia.[ He] died[ at] Salzburg, 27 November,[ 7]89. In[ 1233 he] was canonized[ by] Gregory[ IX].[ His doctrine that] the[ earth is a] sphere was derived from the teaching of ancient ge[ographers],[ and] his belief in the existence[ of] the antipodes was probably influenced by the accounts which the ancient Irish voyagers gave of their journeys. This,[ at least,] is the opinion[ of] Rettberg ("Kirchengesch. Deutschlands", II, 236).

